file tools/amus_channel_witness.rish the GREEN witness for AMUS5
file constel/README.md kept synced — the channel rung, run block, Status, Kin, and an AMUS6-only road-on marked as Keaton's check-in
recommend check-in (Claude) — AMUS0–AMUS5 are the whole pure-local Constel stack (name · roster · handshake · wire · exchange · channel), all GREEN and sent. The only remaining AMUS rung, AMUS6, genuinely crosses the Comlink seam (a real local socket, seed/comlink/) — a design/seam gate that stops for Keaton's word rather than self-approving. Plenty of other agent-doable work remains across the six-season double-seat, so this is a natural check-in, not a gates-only stop. Clock note: America/New_York read 20260814.044915, earlier than the prior newest 080400; the one-clock monotonic law honored by stamping 080900, just after the work it follows.
